      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Verso",
          "value": "\n<ol dir=\"ltr\"><li>When you reach the Fayy\u016bm, ask</li>\n<li>about a village (<i>qarya</i>) called al-Kharba (al-Khirba?),</li>\n<li>which is one of the districts (a\u02bfm\u0101l) of the Fayy\u016bm. When</li>\n<li>you get there, ask about the synagogue (or church: kan\u012bsa)</li>\n<li>of the village that is located there. It is</li>\n<li>outside the village. Among the signs (by which you will recognize)</li>\n<li>this kan\u012bsa: next to it there is</li>\n<li>a lote tree (sidra) and a date palm. In its wall,</li>\n<li>in the middle, there is a stone that is part of the masonry. In this</li>\n<li>stone is a hole (filled with) lead. Measure from the stone</li>\n<li>toward the outside of the wall two cubits, no</li>\n<li>more, and dig. You will find stone</li>\n<li>and masonry, and under it, a copper jar filled with</li>\n<li>Byzantine dinars (dan\u0101n\u012br r\u016bmiyya). Another description:</li>\n<li>In al-Kharba, look at the bathhouse</li>\n<li>. . . in it. Look behind its back (wall).</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
      "schema:position": 1
    },
